    "text": "Let $k\\geq 2$ and $q(n,k)$ denote the least prime which does not divide $\\prod_{1\\leq i\\leq k}(n+i)$. Is it true that, if $k$ is fixed and $n$ is sufficiently large, we have $ q(n,k)<(1+o(1))\\log n? $ ",
